\section{Setup}{

Create an API token on populiva.com under Lab > Developer. Choose the
scopes it needs: \code{read} to look things up, \code{studies} to create and run
studies and review submissions, and \code{money} for bonuses. Then add it to
your \code{.Renviron} file (for example with \code{usethis::edit_r_environ()}):

\if{html}{\out{<div class="sourceCode">}}\preformatted{POPULIVA_TOKEN=pv_...
}\if{html}{\out{</div>}}

Restart R, and check it works with \code{\link[=pv_balance]{pv_balance()}}. Keep the token out of
scripts you share.
}

\section{A typical study}{

\enumerate{
\item \code{\link[=pv_create_study]{pv_create_study()}} with your survey link, then \code{\link[=pv_launch]{pv_launch()}}.
\item In your survey, save \code{PARTICIPANT_ID} from the link, and send people to
\code{\link[=pv_completion_url]{pv_completion_url()}} at the end.
\item \code{\link[=pv_submissions]{pv_submissions()}}, join to your data, then \code{\link[=pv_approve]{pv_approve()}} or
\code{\link[=pv_reject]{pv_reject()}}, and \code{\link[=pv_bonus]{pv_bonus()}} if you promised one.
\item \code{\link[=pv_issue_provenance_report]{pv_issue_provenance_report()}} and cite its URL in your methods.
}

Setup guides for Qualtrics, jsPsych, Gorilla, oTree, PsychoPy and
LimeSurvey are at \url{https://populiva.com/guides}.
